   207	    Parity with the step-15 reader (`.github/scripts/
   208	    validate-pair-rail-verdict.py`, parse_verdict_file), stated at its REAL
   209	    scope: block selection (the regex below is the validator's own — the
   210	    first ```yaml fence, not the first fence of any language) and inline
   211	    comment stripping MATCH; list parsing (`- item`) exists ONLY here —
   212	    parse_verdict_file reads key:value and sub-dicts and would drop
   213	    `delta_allowlist` silently. The W1 server-side port must therefore extend
   214	    ONE shared reader (this file is the declared reference), never grow a
   215	    third parser of the same signed file.
   216	    """
   217	    fields: Dict[str, object] = {}
   218	    block = re.search(r"```yaml[ \t]*\n(.*?)```", text, re.DOTALL)  # t8 P1: ASCII-only, \s swallowed a leading NBSP line
   219	    if block is None:
   220	        # No yaml block -> no fields -> every consumer below fails closed.
   221	        return fields
   222	    cur_list: Optional[str] = None
