   424	    # they only agree on a canonical block. A non-canonical top-level line is
   425	    # refused here rather than handed to two different grammars — E_DECISION
   426	    # because the class this closes is the decision override (`verdict :
   427	    # NO-GO` + `verdict: GO`), and because a refusal that names the decision
   428	    # rail is the one an operator can act on.
